<title>BELGIUM: EU intervention grain stocks rise to 1.24 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>EU intervention grain stocks rise to 1.24 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union intervention grain stocks rose to 1.24 million tonnes net on April 24, from 1.18 million tonnes on April 6, the European Commission said on Monday.</p>
<p>The total included 321,184 tonnes of intervention soft wheat, which rose from 314,263 tonnes during the same period.</p>
<p>Intervention barley stocks also rose slightly to 386,442 tonnes, from 370,104 tonnes between April 6 and April 24.</p>
<p>Intervention rye stocks rose to 534,972 tonnes, from 492,412 tonnes.</p>
<p>EU intervention stocks totalled 2.60 million tonnes at the start of the 1996/97 (July/June) season. The total included 458,978 tonnes of soft wheat, 1.34 million tonnes of barley and 793,261 tonnes of rye.</p>
<p>European Union intervention grain stocks (tonnes)</p>
<p>		    24/4/97	6/4/97	  1/7/96</p>
<p> All cereals     1,244,299   1,178,462     2,596,112</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p> Soft wheat	  321,184     314,263	 458,978</p>
<p> Durum wheat	    nil	  nil	     nil</p>
<p> Barley		386,442     370,104	1,343,870</p>
<p> Rye		   534,972     492,412	  793,261</p>
<p> Maize		   1,701	 1,701		  3</p>
<p> Sorghum		  nil	   nil		nil</p>
<p> Triticale		nil	   nil		nil</p>
<p>NB: Figures are net after deduction of domestic and export sales commitments</p>
